WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:19.820
What it do, y'all? This week we
crazy in love with "Gone Girl" by Gillian Flynn.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.340
It’s been five years since Nick Dunne hit da jackpot by puttin a ring on Amy Elliott —

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.440
a girl who almost as fine as she is rich.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.140
But what was supposed to be anotha depressing anniversary celebratin a dead-ass marriage

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.560
turns in to a full on sh*tshow when Amy goes missing.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.720
Where dat girl go?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.780
Now there’s somethin I gotta cover real quick:

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.280
this book ain’t just narrated by one fool tellin us what's up with the Dunnes. Naw.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.360
We gettin da lowdown from two different sources — Amy and Nick.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.500
And at first, Amy conversatin wit us through her journal.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.920
Dat journal make it sound like things were real legit between them, in the beginning,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.740
but da party don't last too long.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.680
Nick loses his job like a scrub,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.140
makes em leave their life of swank city-livin and move to da boonies of Missouri to care for his mama,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.320
and then uses Amy’s inherited ends to open up a bar with his sista.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.860
Not only dat, but according to da journal, Nick been whoopin on Amy lately, and she scurred for her life.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.040
Anyway, when da popo hit da scene, erryone start suspectin Nick of killin Amy.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.020
I mean, ain’t you eva seen da news?
Da husband always did it. 'Cept OJ, I guess...

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.560
But when more and more evidence start pilin up against him,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.060
da media gets a big ol’ sensationalism boner and start hatin on Nick like he da killer fo real.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.040
Turns out, Amy ain’t even dead.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.620
Matta fact, girl faked her own death, wrote a bunk-ass diary lyin her ass off,

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.920
and left a whole buncha clues to make Nick look guilty — all cuz he's been cheatin on her like a dick.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.400
Nick soon figure out his wife is alive and jus tryna burn him —

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.340
but how’s a brotha gonna prove it to the dumbass police?

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.800
Nick take some of da heat off by
playin da game dat Amy playin.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.740
Brotha start workin it to make sho public opinion is on his side by showin his mug on TV,

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.260
runnin his mouth bout how bad a husband he was,

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.960
and sayin he jus miss his baby girl and want her to come back home.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.220
As for Amy, her master plan gets sh*t on when when some trailer trash honkies boost all her cash.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:14.660
Now she ain’t got no choice but to hit up her first boy toy, Desi, who been prayin fo a crack at dat ass fo years.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.580
Da tables turn on Amy, though,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:22.300
who realize dat Desi jus wanna control her like almost every otha dude she ever met — 'cept Nick.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.320
Eventually, she tired of bein holed up in
his swag pad,

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:32.360
so girl slices dat fool up and runs back to Nick, tellin da media that Desi was behind her whole disappearance.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.020
Some messed up sh*t, right? But at least my man, Nick, is off da hook.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:40.560
Nick know he gotta get his ass far
from this crazy biddy, and even start to choke a b*tch.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.860
But brotha stop when he realize his
life would be way too empty without her.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:50.100
Still, he does wanna stop Amy from bonin up anyone else’s life and plans to expose da truth.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.160
But Amy one step ahead of him: girl
impregnates herself with his love juice,

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.200
leftover from tissues, porn, and otha sh*t.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.320
Fo real!

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.480
To top it off, she say,

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.560
“Look playboy, you even dare try to come forward wit yo story,

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.180
who knows what's gonna happen to yo baby boy.”

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.760
Damn, girl! You crazy!

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.680
So in the end, Nick and Amy stay
togetha, with Amy keepin his ass in check,

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.980
and Nick spendin his days thinkin how righteous it would be to kill this b*tch. Man.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.560
Nick’s lawyer said it best: “’You two are the most f**ked up people I have ever met,

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:27.200
and I specialize in f**ked up people.”

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.560
Whew! This book makes my nuts shrivel up.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:33.280
See, most love stories gonna drop some romantic rhymes on yo ass,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.680
sayin dat love is da baddest and sweetest sh*t you’ll eva know.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.540
But Fynn ain’t playin no fairy tale game. Naw, blood.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.960
Da book’s epigraph set da stage fo somethin way mo fu**ed up:

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:48.780
“Love is the world’s infinite mutability;
lies, hatred, murder even, are all knit up

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:54.460
in it; it is the inevitable blossoming of its opposites, a magnificent rose smelling faintly of blood.”

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.760
Real love means da whole package — 
not jus' the smiles, da laughs, and da good times;

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.520
love got a darker side, too.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:06.540
Dat's why instead of jus' describin love with images of sunshine, happiness, and roses,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.140
Flynn talks bout nuclear explosions, cancer, and my fave — thorns.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:11.920
Check it out:

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.680
"Nick and I fit together. I am a little too much, and he is a little too little.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.860
￼I am a thornbush, bristling from the overattention of my parents,

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:24.500
and he is a man of a million little fatherly stab wounds, and my thorns fit perfectly into them.”

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.080
So on da one hand, we got a symbol of love where two peeps perfectly complement each otha.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.780
But at da same time, dat complement all about thorns foreva jabbing into open wounds.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.360
God. Damn.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.580
Anotha one of "Gone Girl’s" main jams
is narrative,

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.060
and how reality is all in da power of da homie holdin da pen, mic, or camera.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:48.580
Like Amy’s pops say on page 190, “The truth is malleable; you just need to pick the right expert.”

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.660
We livin’ in a world where there be so many images flashin in front of our eyes 24/7,

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.140
dat da truth can get lost in all the bullsh*t.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.460
Ain’t nobody realize this mo than Amy.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:02.660
Girl always creatin fake narratives in line with what da media wanna believe,

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.240
in order to f**k wit Nick and get her way.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.240
For example, she makes some bullsh*t bout Nick bein a wife-beater in her journal,

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.000
but since da “abusive husband” is a character dat da media gets hard for,

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.140
they eat it up, and what’s true don’t even matta no mo.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:22.700
But da truth ain’t da only thing dat get lost in our world of sensationalist media sh*tstorms — our identities do, too.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.980
The title “Gone Girl” ain’t only reppin da fact that Amy’s physical body went missing,

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:30.500
but also dat who she is has been gone for a long time.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.420
Cuz of this jacked-up world, she been:

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:37.720
"Amazing Amy. Preppy ‘80s Girl. Ultimate-Frisbee Granola and Blushing Ingenue

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:44.160
and Witty Hepburnian Sophisticate. Brainy Ironic Girl and Boho Babe (the latest version of Frisbee Granola).

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:50.320
Cool Girl and Loved Wife and Unloved Wife and Vengeful Scorned Wife. Diary Amy.”

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.960
People been exposed to so many
narratives, like the corrupt politician,

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:59.020
the lazy trust fund baby, or da violent gangsta-lookin dude, dat there ain’t no room for self.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.220
And the scurriest thing is: when you gettin marginalized and defined 24/7,

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:08.780
you sometimes find that you become exactly the kinda monster dat errybody makin you out to be.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.220
Hell, just look at Nick!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:14.460
Eventually, he does physically abuse his wife and fantasize about icin her.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.540
That’s some messed up sh*t right there, man.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:21.200
“It’s a very difficult era in which to be a person, just a real, actual person,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:25.900
instead of a collection of personality traits selected from an endless automat of characters.”

